1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:06,684
This is Fretlane: a free, open-source guitar tab player where the whole band plays along.

2
00:00:07,134 --> 00:00:09,732
Here's a quick tour of everything it does.

3
00:00:10,582 --> 00:00:16,496
Your library starts out full: twenty-two well-known songs, arranged for the whole band.

4
00:00:16,646 --> 00:00:21,286
Each one is tagged by level, so you can start with the beginner songs.

5
00:00:21,436 --> 00:00:24,457
Or search by title, artist or tag.

6
00:00:25,083 --> 00:00:30,628
Open a song and press play. The whole band plays, and the cursor follows every note.

7
00:00:34,451 --> 00:00:39,722
Click a track to read that part: the bass line, the drums, or back to the melody.

8
00:00:45,527 --> 00:00:50,008
Solo or mute any instrument to hear exactly what it plays.

9
00:00:52,064 --> 00:00:54,681
Zoom in when you need a closer look.

10
00:00:57,264 --> 00:01:02,330
Too fast? Slow it down, from a quarter of the speed up to one and a half times.

11
00:01:05,522 --> 00:01:10,429
To drill a tricky passage, drag across the bars and press L to loop them.

12
00:01:10,579 --> 00:01:14,387
Add a count-in, and a click track that follows the tab.

13
00:01:14,537 --> 00:01:19,288
Now it counts you in, and keeps repeating those bars until you have them.

14
00:01:29,920 --> 00:01:35,582
The metronome sets itself to the song's tempo, at your practice speed, in one click.

15
00:01:37,145 --> 00:01:39,735
Pick eighths, triplets or sixteenths.

16
00:01:41,534 --> 00:01:43,636
Or tap in any tempo you like.

17
00:01:51,121 --> 00:01:55,560
Star the songs you're working on, and find them all under Favorites.

18
00:02:00,105 --> 00:02:05,639
Learned a song? Mark it as done and it moves to the archive. One click brings it back.

19
00:02:07,689 --> 00:02:13,522
Add your own tabs: a Guitar Pro or MusicXML file, or a link to one.

20
00:02:13,672 --> 00:02:17,991
Or paste a plain-text tab, the kind you find all over the web.

21
00:02:19,298 --> 00:02:24,071
Fretlane turns it into a real tab you can play, slow down and loop.

22
00:02:26,098 --> 00:02:31,121
Text tabs don't carry rhythm, so the timing inside a bar is a best guess.

23
00:02:32,664 --> 00:02:37,808
Link a YouTube video, and the tab follows the recording, bar by bar.

24
00:02:41,914 --> 00:02:46,170
Switch between lead, rhythm and bass while the video keeps playing.

25
00:02:51,514 --> 00:02:56,831
To set it up, pause the video on the first beat, and pin bar one to that moment.

26
00:02:57,281 --> 00:03:03,491
If the band speeds up or slows down, pin more bars, or tap along on every downbeat.

27
00:03:03,941 --> 00:03:08,214
Spotify tracks work the same way, always at normal speed.

28
00:03:09,064 --> 00:03:13,698
Fretlane is a normal desktop app for Mac, Windows and Linux.

29
00:03:14,148 --> 00:03:20,450
Your songs are plain files in a folder on your own computer. No account, nothing uploaded.

30
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:25,449
It's free and open source. The download link is in the description.
